polaris (1.0.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: taskbar system monitor showing live CPU usage, CPU
    temperature, memory and swap usage, and the network transfer rate.
  * Control centre page for choosing which readings are shown and how often
    they refresh, stored with DConfig.
  * Ending a process now checks the target's start time as well as its name and
    signals through a pidfd, so a recycled pid cannot be hit.
  * New polaris-sensord package: a small sandboxed service that publishes the
    readings the kernel keeps to root (the CPU package power counter) as named
    values under /run/polaris/sensors, for the dock item to pick up.
  * The graphics card's power draw through NVML, listed next to the cpu package in
    the panel.
  * Fan gauges are drawn against the chip's ceiling (fan*_max) or the configured
    fanScaleRpm, and the fan list is labelled.
  * Power draw and fan speed from hwmon and the powercap energy counter, each
    with its own dock-line switch and a card in the detail panel.
  * Swap has its own bar in the panel instead of a slice of the memory bar, and
    is listed with its own reading and percentage.
  * The dock item can draw the history of each reading under its number, so the
    taskbar shows where a reading is going and not only where it is: numbers with
    charts under them, or charts with labels only, chosen for the whole line in
    the control centre. Each chart is scaled to what it measures and is sized
    from its cells, so the item still cannot jitter.
  * Clicking the item opens a detail panel: cpu breakdown, per-core bars,
    memory split, transfer history charts and the busiest processes, in its own
    layer-shell window that follows the light or dark theme.

